# MCP tool server (TypeScript)

## Project facts (edit these)
- Runtime: Node 20+, ESM (`"type": "module"`)
- SDK: `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` (`McpServer` + `StdioServerTransport` or `StreamableHTTPServerTransport`)
- Schema library: `zod` (the SDK accepts zod shapes for tool inputs)
- Entry point: `src/index.ts`
- Test: `npm test` · Lint: `npm run lint` · Typecheck: `npx tsc --noEmit`

## Before you say "done"
- `npm test`, `npm run lint` and `npx tsc --noEmit` all pass.
- `npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector node dist/index.js` lists every tool and each sample call returns structured content.

## Tool design
- One tool, one job. Name tools `verb_noun` in snake_case (`search_issues`, `read_file`).
- The description says WHEN the model should pick this tool, in 1–2 sentences, not only what it does.
- Every input is a `zod` field with `.describe()`. Prefer `z.enum([...])` to free-text when the value set is known.
- Bound every input: `.max()` on strings, `.int().min().max()` on numbers, allow-lists for hosts and base paths.
- Return compact structured results. Truncate large outputs and state that they were truncated and how to page.
- Do not return more than the caller asked for; summarize lists and expose an `offset`/`cursor` input instead.

## Errors
- Validation and runtime failures return `{ content: [{ type: "text", text: "<actionable message>" }], isError: true }`.
- Never leak stack traces, file system paths outside the sandbox, or secret values in error text.
- Map upstream HTTP failures to a short cause plus what the model can change (`"rate limited; retry after 30s"`).

## stdio hygiene
- With the stdio transport, `stdout` is the protocol channel. Log ONLY to `stderr` (`console.error`) — one stray `console.log` corrupts the stream.
- No interactive prompts, no TTY assumptions; the server runs headless under a client.
- Handle `SIGINT`/`SIGTERM` by closing the transport before exit.

## Security
- Secrets come from environment variables only; never hard-code, log or echo them in tool output.
- Resolve and check every path against an allowed root (`path.resolve` + prefix check) before reading or writing.
- Tools that delete, write or send must say so in the description and require an explicit `confirm: true` input.
- Outbound HTTP only to an allow-list of hosts; set timeouts and a response-size cap.

## Boundaries
- Do not edit generated files or the lockfile by hand.
- Do not add a dependency for something under ~30 lines of code.
- Keep the server's public tool list stable; rename only with a deprecation note in the README.

## Definition of done
- Each new or changed tool has a test that calls it THROUGH the server (`Client` + `InMemoryTransport`), not only the handler function.
- The README tool table (name, when to use, inputs) is updated whenever a tool is added, renamed or removed.
